## Q2. Why are you leaving current company or internship?

### Answer

My internship period is ending, and I am now looking for a full-time role where I can continue learning and take more responsibility. There is no full-time opening there, so I am looking for an opportunity where I can grow professionally and contribute to the organization.

---

## Q3. Why do you want to join our company?

### Answer

This role fits my skills, and I want to grow with your company. Your company provides a good learning environment and works on technologies that match my interests and abilities. I believe this is the right place to start my career and build my future.

---

## Q4. Why should we hire you?

### Answer

You should hire me because I am a quick learner, hardworking, and ready to learn and contribute to the team. I have a strong foundation in Java and I am passionate about software development. I am sincere, adaptable, and ready to work hard to grow with the company.

---

## Q5. What are your strengths and weakness?

### Strengths

- Quick learner
- Hardworking
- Problem-solving mindset
- Interested in Java and backend development
- Consistent in learning and practicing coding

### Weakness

I sometimes spend extra time to make sure my work is correct and accurate. This helps me avoid mistakes, but I am improving my speed and learning to manage time better while prioritizing tasks.

### Sample answer

My strengths are problem-solving, quick learning, and consistency. I have a strong interest in Java and practice coding regularly. My weakness is that I sometimes focus too much on details, but I am learning to improve my speed and manage my time better.

---

## Q6. Where do you see yourself in the next five years?

### Answer

In the next five years, I want to keep learning continuously, improve my technical skills, and grow along with the company. I want to become a valuable contributor and take on more responsibility in a professional environment.

---

## Q7. What is your expected salary?

### Answer

As a fresher, I am expecting a salary that is in line with company standards and my skills. I am more focused on learning and growth, and I am open to a fair offer based on the role and company policy.

